# CLTS clears CR0.TS (bit 3); every other CR0 bit, PG included, and all
# flags stay put. It needs CPL 0 (#GP(0) above it and in virtual-8086
# mode; real mode runs at level 0). When TS is already clear nothing
# changes, so the step retires without a CR0 write.
require_ring0
read_msw32 status
bit ts status 3
not clear ts
retire_if clear
const keep 32 4294967287
and value status keep
write_control 0 value
preserve_flags all
retire
